# The lifecycle of the Maven service demo in one private scratch repository,
# building with kaniko: the k3s campaigns' profile, private and kaniko on the
# ordinary runner, for the linked flow lifecycle-forgejo.cases runs public
# with Buildah. The kaniko job image is the campaign's, labelled for the
# consumer trial's layer repository, which every event of the trial, the
# lifecycle included, runs its workflows from. Prepare with forgejo=<this
# file> and job-image=java:<reviewed local image>; CI_JOB_IMAGE is also the
# Java image the snapshot builds the service with. From the caller,
# FORGE_CI_LIVE_CONSUMER_VISIBILITY=private and
# FORGE_CI_LIVE_FORGEJO_IMAGE_BUILDER=kaniko. The service's readiness runs the
# published image with Podman, so the lab needs the contract's
# container/readiness runner whichever builder builds the image: Forge Lab's
# Compose road with its full-release runners, not k3s. amd64 runners only for
# now.
#
#   just campaign-lane <dir> forgejo test/live/campaigns/lifecycle-private-forgejo.cases
setting visibility=private
setting image-builder=kaniko
setting admin-lint=false
setting admin-vulnerabilities=false
setting admin-application-tests=false
setting admin-reproducible-builds=false

consumer hello-maven-service lifecycle CI_JOB_IMAGE=@JOB_IMAGE_JAVA RELEASE_PLATFORMS=linux/amd64 CI_IMAGE_BUILDER=kaniko CI_IMAGE_BUILDER_JOB_IMAGE=@KANIKO_JOB_IMAGE
